WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.074 --> 00:00:16.342
"Wow!" Cole exclaimed.

2
00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:18.184
"That's awesome, Nathan.

3
00:00:18.804 --> 00:00:20.725
The judges really like your painting!"

4
00:00:21.786 --> 00:00:23.427
But Patrick was frowning at Owen.

5
00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:25.809
"Are you sure you heard the judges right?"

6
00:00:26.049 --> 00:00:26.750
he demanded.

7
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.532
"Did they mention my painting?"

8
00:00:30.492 --> 00:00:31.233
Owen shrugged.

9
00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:32.694
"Not while I was listening."

10
00:00:33.795 --> 00:00:34.636
Maggie smirked.

11
00:00:34.656 --> 00:00:37.078
"Too bad, Patrick," she said.

12
00:00:37.098 --> 00:00:38.680
"Come on, guys.

13
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.662
We'd better get back to the lemonade stand."

14
00:00:41.723 --> 00:00:43.064
Henry and Cole followed her.

15
00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:46.487
"Do you think Nathan might actually win?"

16
00:00:46.727 --> 00:00:47.468
Cole asked.

17
00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:49.149
Henry shrugged.

18
00:00:49.169 --> 00:00:49.990
"He might.

19
00:00:50.671 --> 00:00:52.152
His painting is really good."

20
00:00:53.173 --> 00:00:56.056
Near the lemonade stand the fiddler had finished his performance.

21
00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:00.691
Now several bongo drummers were setting up their equipment on the bandstand.

22
00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:04.613
"It looks like we don't have any customers," Cole said.

23
00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:06.775
"Want to check out the crafts fair?"

24
00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:09.036
"Sure," Henry said.

25
00:01:09.056 --> 00:01:11.138
"Okay," Maggie agreed.

26
00:01:11.158 --> 00:01:13.419
"But we shouldn't stay away for long.

27
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.262
We'll probably have more customers when the music starts up again."

28
00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:21.005
The crafts fair was crowded and colorful.

29
00:01:21.865 --> 00:01:25.748
There were lots of interesting handmade items for sale everywhere Henry looked.

30
00:01:27.028 --> 00:01:30.129
Some of the booths featured demonstrations or classes too.

31
00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:34.030
Henry stopped to watch a woman churning butter by hand.

32
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.571
Meanwhile Maggie waved at someone in the basket-weaving booth across the way.

33
00:01:38.591 --> 00:01:40.812
"Look," Maggie said.

34
00:01:40.832 --> 00:01:42.012
"There's Hannah."

35
00:01:42.992 --> 00:01:48.514
A dark-haired girl was sitting on a stool, weaving grasses into the shape of a large, flat basket.

36
00:01:49.574 --> 00:01:51.855
She looked up when The Lemonade Detectives approached.

37
00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:55.936
"Oh hi," Hannah said, pushing her hair out of her eyes.

38
00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:57.889
"It's the lemonade gang."

39
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.633
"Hi." Maggie smiled at Hannah, looking at the basket in Hannah's lap.

40
00:02:02.653 --> 00:02:05.976
"Your parents have a booth every year, don't they?"

41
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:07.658
Hannah nodded.

42
00:02:07.678 --> 00:02:10.820
"They look forward to Belltown Arts Day all year.

43
00:02:11.781 --> 00:02:15.564
They love showing off their baskets and teaching people about weaving."

44
00:02:16.585 --> 00:02:17.786
She pointed into the booth.

45
00:02:18.907 --> 00:02:22.170
Her parents were helping a young boy weave a small, round basket.

46
00:02:23.151 --> 00:02:24.292
Henry stepped inside.

47
00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:28.186
The booth was filled with baskets of every size, shape, and color.

48
00:02:28.206 --> 00:02:30.508
"Wow," Henry said.

49
00:02:30.528 --> 00:02:32.989
"These baskets are really cool."

50
00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:34.530
Cole grinned.

51
00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.792
"Look, this one has a picture of a cat woven into it," he said.

52
00:02:38.812 --> 00:02:40.954
"Just like Nathan's painting!

53
00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.474
Did you make it, Hannah?"

54
00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:44.155
She nodded.

55
00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:45.336
"I love cats."

56
00:02:45.356 --> 00:02:48.898
"You should enter it in the art show," said Maggie.

57
00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:50.679
Hannah frowned.

58
00:02:51.039 --> 00:02:51.720
"No way.

59
00:02:52.396 --> 00:02:56.938
Those snobby art people don't want anything from the crafts booths in their contest.

60
00:02:57.898 --> 00:03:02.420
That's why the organizers made sure the crafts show was stuck way over here at the opposite end

61
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.041
of the park."

62
00:03:04.341 --> 00:03:05.442
Henry was surprised.

63
00:03:06.142 --> 00:03:07.603
Hannah sounded really annoyed.

64
00:03:07.623 --> 00:03:11.544
"Not all artists are snobby," Maggie reminded Hannah.

65
00:03:11.564 --> 00:03:14.105
"Our friend Nathan is really nice.

66
00:03:15.106 --> 00:03:18.107
He's a painter who might win the Under Twelve category this year."

67
00:03:19.068 --> 00:03:19.868
Hannah shrugged.

68
00:03:20.552 --> 00:03:23.593
"Whatever," she muttered, staring at the basket in her lap.

69
00:03:24.713 --> 00:03:28.054
Cole was digging through a bin full of small, colorful baskets.

70
00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.315
"Hey, how much is this one?"

71
00:03:30.535 --> 00:03:32.516
he asked, holding up one of the baskets.

72
00:03:33.596 --> 00:03:35.957
"I just remembered my mom's birthday is next week.

73
00:03:36.637 --> 00:03:38.597
She loves handmade stuff like this."

74
00:03:39.678 --> 00:03:43.199
Hannah told him the price, and Cole dug some money out of his pocket.

75
00:03:44.339 --> 00:03:47.040
Meanwhile Maggie grabbed Henry's phone to check the time.

76
00:03:48.012 --> 00:03:52.635
"Come on, you guys," she said as Hannah slipped Cole's basket into a small shopping bag.

77
00:03:52.655 --> 00:03:55.477
"We should get back to the lemonade stand."

78
00:03:55.497 --> 00:03:57.719
"Okay," Henry said.

79
00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:59.080
"See you, Hannah."

80
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.462
"Bye," Hannah said.

81
00:04:01.482 --> 00:04:05.024
"Maybe I'll come by for some lemonade later if I have time."

82
00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:13.630
Back at the lemonade stand, Henry and the others were busy for a while serving thirsty customers.

83
00:04:14.631 --> 00:04:15.852
They knew all the customers.

84
00:04:16.544 --> 00:04:17.944
But then a stranger appeared.

85
00:04:19.105 --> 00:04:23.066
She was a very tall, very thin woman dressed in a shiny green dress.

86
00:04:24.226 --> 00:04:28.788
Her bright red hair was piled high atop her head and held in place with sparkly barrettes.

87
00:04:29.928 --> 00:04:32.729
Enormous white-framed sunglasses covered half her face.

88
00:04:32.749 --> 00:04:38.250
"One lemonade, please," she said, setting a quarter on the table.

89
00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.191
"Coming right up."

90
00:04:40.411 --> 00:04:41.511
Henry picked up a pitcher.

91
00:04:41.531 --> 00:04:43.912
"And welcome to Belltown."

92
00:04:44.908 --> 00:04:47.589
The woman peered at him over the top of her sunglasses.

93
00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.950
Her eyes were suspicious.

94
00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.331
"What do you mean by that?"

95
00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:53.351
she demanded.

96
00:04:53.372 --> 00:04:56.173
"How do you know I don't live here?"

97
00:04:57.193 --> 00:04:59.834
Henry traded a surprised look with Maggie and Cole.

98
00:04:59.854 --> 00:05:02.935
"It was a guess," Henry replied.

99
00:05:02.955 --> 00:05:06.357
"Because we know almost everybody in town."

100
00:05:06.377 --> 00:05:08.678
"Yeah," Cole added.

101
00:05:08.698 --> 00:05:10.799
"Belltown is not very big."

102
00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:13.960
"How did you hear about Belltown Arts Day?"

103
00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.341
Maggie asked the woman.

104
00:05:15.361 --> 00:05:17.802
"I didn't think it was very famous."

105
00:05:17.822 --> 00:05:22.685
"Famous? What would someone like you know about being famous?"

106
00:05:23.045 --> 00:05:23.946
the woman snapped.

107
00:05:25.007 --> 00:05:26.888
Suddenly she spun around and rushed away.

108
00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:29.549
Cole stared after her.

109
00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:31.491
"What a weirdo!"

110
00:05:31.511 --> 00:05:35.353
"Yeah." Maggie picked up the quarter the woman had left.

111
00:05:36.554 --> 00:05:38.115
"She didn't even wait for her lemonade."

112
00:05:39.055 --> 00:05:40.056
Henry didn't answer.

113
00:05:40.808 --> 00:05:44.293
He'd just noticed Nathan rushing toward them, looking very upset.

114
00:05:45.354 --> 00:05:47.557
Nathan skidded to a stop in front of the stand.

115
00:05:47.577 --> 00:05:49.740
"My painting," he cried.

116
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.502
"It's gone!"
